Banner Kings — Redux: Licensing Notice
=======================================

Banner Kings is the work of R-Vaccari and the original Banner Kings
contributors. The upstream repository
(https://github.com/R-Vaccari/bannerlord-banner-kings) does not declare a
license. By default this means the upstream code is "all rights reserved"
under copyright law, and the original author retains exclusive rights over
its distribution and modification.

This fork (Banner Kings — Redux) is published in good faith to keep the mod
working on current Bannerlord builds and to add native War Sails / Nord
integration, while the upstream project has been inactive for an extended
period. We have NOT received explicit permission from R-Vaccari to fork
or redistribute Banner Kings, and we make no claim that the upstream code
is BSD-licensed, MIT-licensed, or otherwise open-source.

Conditions of this fork
-----------------------

1. All credit for the original Banner Kings, including all of its design,
   code, content, XML data, art, and structure, belongs to R-Vaccari and
   the original Banner Kings contributors.

2. If R-Vaccari (or any of the original authors) requests that this fork
   be taken down, for any reason and at any time, it will be removed
   immediately, without question, without delay, and without argument.

3. Modifications introduced specifically by this fork (the Bannerlord
   1.3.x compatibility port, the War Sails / Nord integration, the
   seafaring lifestyles, the Nordic Thrall Law, the build/deploy
   tooling, and other Redux-only additions) are made available under
   the same conditions as the upstream code: pending the original
   author's permission, with no separate license claim.

4. Redistribution of this fork is permitted only insofar as the upstream
   project's implicit terms permit it. Anyone redistributing this fork
   does so at their own risk, and remains bound by the original author's
   rights over the upstream code.

This file replaces an earlier version that incorrectly attributed the
upstream Banner Kings to the BSD 3-Clause License. The earlier file was
inaccurate; the upstream project has no such license declared, and the
correction is documented here for the record.
